  <h1>Teaching</h1>
  <p>I’ve been a teaching assistant at UCF since August 2025. I lead weekly lab sessions for more than 150 students, and I work the problems as live code instead of slides — it’s slower, and it shows the mistakes, which is the point.</p>
  <p>Office hours are the other half of it. Most of what happens there is one student, one bug, and a question they’d rather not ask in front of the room. I also grade assignments and exams, and I try hard to grade the same way across every section — a score shouldn’t depend on which TA opened the submission.</p>
  <h2>Courses I’ve supported</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Data Structures & Algorithms 1</li>
    <li>Data Structures & Algorithms 2</li>
    <li>Senior Design 1</li>
    <li>Cryptography</li>
  </ul>
